+// The content cache's budget: this (halved when video memory runs out) times the upscaling's factor, as upscaled
+// textures are factor^2 times larger: 4x let 128 MiB hold a fraction of a room's textures, evicted and upscaled
+// again while it played (Rogueport's plaza with the Paper Mario 64 bosses: 378 of 688 upscales the same picture
+// again). The memory guards step the upscaling down (and so this) when memory runs short.
+uint64_t s_contentBudgetBase = texture::ContentCacheBudgetBytes;
+uint64_t content_cache_budget() noexcept {
